  "question": {
    "text": "The TV transmission tower at a particular station has a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>125</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. For doubling the coverage of its range, the height of the tower should be increased by"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>375</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>125</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Maximum distance covered is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msqrt></math>, here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is the radius.</p><p>Now, to increase the length of radio transmission to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;times,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mi>R</mi></msqrt></math></p><p>Height of tower is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>125</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>\n\\(\\begin{aligned} \\Delta H=h^{\\prime}-h &=500-125 \\\\ &=375 \\end{aligned}\\)"
  }
